<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="3d" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>3D</title>

    <introduction>
        <p>
            I do a ton of 3D design.
            Here, I'll list as much as I can recall.
        </p>
    </introduction>

    <subsection xml:id="uai">
        <title>Unreal Authorized Instructor (UAI)</title>

        <p>
            As the title suggests, I have been certified by the Education &amp;
            Training Partners Team at Epic Games in my ability to teach Unreal
            Engine.
        </p>

        <figure xml:id="img_uai">
            <caption>UAI</caption>
            <image source="UAI/7c1622e2-74c9-4ae4-84f2-f1bdb8f1bfa2.png" width="25%">
                <shortdescription>UAI Badge</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </figure>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="igda_iiitd">
        <title>International Game Developers Association (IGDA)</title>

        <p>
            I am the current co-chair for the IIIT Delhi student chapter of the
            (IGDA), which is the world's largest nonprofit membership
            organization serving all individuals who create games.
        </p>

        <figure>
            <caption>IGDA IIIT Delhi</caption>
            <image source="igda/igda_logo.png" width="25%">
                <description>
                    <p>
                        Our logo
                    </p>
                </description>
            </image>
        </figure>

        <p>
            You can join our
            <url href="https://discord.gg/muZEEAHsg6">official Discord server</url>
            which is an informal place to talk everything game dev related.
            Additionally, our website is
            <url href="https://igda.org/chapters/india-iiit-delhi/"/>.
            More work done for this is listed in <xref ref="club-events"/>.
        </p>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="gamedev">
        <title>Game Development with Unreal Engine</title>

        <p>
            I taught Unreal Engine in my university during the summer to about
            100 students.
        </p>

        <figure>
            <caption>Some images from the course</caption>
            <stack>
                <image source="gamedev/gd1.jpeg"/>
                <image source="gamedev/gd2.jpeg"/>
                <image source="gamedev/gd3.jpeg"/>
            </stack>
        </figure>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="artstation">
        <title>ArtStation</title>

        <p>
            I maintain a collection of my work done in Blender, Unreal Engine,
            Designer and more on
            <url href="https://artstation.com/taraash">my ArtStation</url>.
        </p>

        <p>
            Some recent work:
        </p>

        <figure>
            <caption>Henfield Part 1</caption>
            <image source="artstation/house.png">
                <description>
                    <p>
                        House in Blender and environment in Unreal
                    </p>
                </description>
            </image>
        </figure>

        <figure>
            <caption>Henfield Part 2</caption>
            <image source="artstation/env.png">
                <description>
                    <p>
                        Buildings in Blender via GN and environment in Unreal
                        via PCG
                    </p>
                </description>
            </image>
        </figure>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="3daf">
        <title>3D Animation and Filmmaking</title>

        <p>
            I've been teaching Blender and related tools as part of the 3D
            animation and filmmaking course in our university for the past two
            offerings.
            Taught more than 50 students, hopefully they all actually enjoyed
            it!
        </p>
    </subsection>
</section>